<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Candidate matrix — review</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ css_rel }}">
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">

  <header class="review-header">
    <div>
      <h1>Candidate matrix</h1>
      <div class="subtitle">Stage 4 — triple selection &amp; gating</div>
    </div>
    <div class="counts">
      <span class="proposed">proposed <span class="num">{{ counts.proposed }}</span></span>
      <span class="approved">approved <span class="num">{{ counts.approved }}</span></span>
      <span class="rejected">rejected <span class="num">{{ counts.rejected }}</span></span>
      <span class="needs_revision">needs_revision <span class="num">{{ counts.needs_revision }}</span></span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="toplinks">
    <a href="locations.html">locations</a>
    <a href="indices.html">indices</a>
    <a href="colormaps.html">colormaps</a>
    <a class="active" href="candidates.html">candidates</a>
  </nav>

  <div class="process-banner">
    <h3>Review workflow</h3>
    <p>Each row groups the colormap variants for one <strong>location × index</strong>
    so you compare palettes side by side. Plates use the per-index
    <em>global</em> normalization (one range across the book). Toggle
    <kbd>CVD</kbd> on a card to preview approximate
    <em>{{ cvd_kind }}</em> color vision. Gate on: washed-out / low range
    coverage, gamut risk (print-safety tag), colormap mismatched with the
    data's pivot, and colorblind legibility.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Scan each location×index row.</strong> Reject duds; keep the
        palette(s) that read best and vary across the book.</li>
      <li><strong>Click <kbd>more</kbd></strong> for the histogram, summary
        stats, range coverage, and pairing provenance.</li>
      <li><strong>Edit <code>config/candidates.yaml</code></strong> — set
        <code>status:</code> to <code>approved</code> / <code>rejected</code> /
        <code>needs_revision</code>. Each card copies its id snippet.</li>
      <li><strong>Re-run <code>spectralcular candidates review --no-fetch</code></strong>
        to refresh pills from cache (~seconds). Use <code>--refresh</code> to
        recolorize, or <code>--only &lt;location_id&gt;</code> to re-fetch one
        location's imagery.</li>
      <li><strong>Then</strong> <code>spectralcular candidates order --auto</code> to
        sequence and <code>spectralcular candidates lock</code> to emit the merge sheet.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  {% for g in groups %}
  <section class="theme-section">
    <h2 class="theme-title">{{ g.theme }}</h2>
    {% for sg in g.subgroups %}
    <div class="li-group">
      <div class="li-head">
        <span class="li-loc">{{ sg.location_name }}</span>
        <span class="li-index">{{ sg.index_name }}</span>
        <span class="li-norm">{{ sg.norm_desc }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cmap-row">
        {% for c in sg.cards %}
        <div class="ccard" id="{{ c.entry.id }}">
          <div class="hero">
            {% if c.thumb_rel %}
              <img class="plate" src="{{ c.thumb_rel }}" alt="{{ c.index_name }} · {{ c.colormap_short }}" loading="lazy">
              {% if c.cvd_rel %}<img class="plate cvd" src="{{ c.cvd_rel }}" alt="CVD-simulated" loading="lazy">{% endif %}
            {% else %}
              <div class="empty">{{ c.error or 'cache miss' }}</div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          <div class="body">
            <div class="header-row">
              <h3 title="{{ c.colormap_short }}">{{ c.colormap_short }}</h3>
              <span class="status {{ c.status }}">{{ c.status }}</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dots">
              <span class="dot {% if c.print_safety == 'safe' %}ok{% elif c.print_safety == 'watchlist' %}warn{% elif c.print_safety == 'unsafe' %}bad{% endif %}"
                    title="print-safety: {{ c.print_safety }}">●</span>
              {% if c.coverage_pct is not none %}
              <span class="dot {% if c.coverage_pct >= 50 %}ok{% elif c.coverage_pct >= 25 %}warn{% else %}bad{% endif %}"
                    title="range coverage {{ '%.0f' % c.coverage_pct }}% of global span">●</span>
              {% endif %}
              <span class="tag type">{{ c.colormap_type }}</span>
              {% if c.cvd_rel %}<button class="cvd-toggle" onclick="this.closest('.ccard').classList.toggle('show-cvd')">CVD</button>{% endif %}
            </div>

            <details class="more">
              <summary>more</summary>
              {% if c.hist_rel %}<div class="hist"><img src="{{ c.hist_rel }}" alt="histogram"></div>{% endif %}
              {% if c.stats %}
              <div class="statline">
                min {{ '%.2f' % c.stats.min }} · p1 {{ '%.2f' % c.stats.p1 }} ·
                med {{ '%.2f' % c.stats.p50 }} · p99 {{ '%.2f' % c.stats.p99 }} ·
                max {{ '%.2f' % c.stats.max }}
              </div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if c.coverage_pct is not none %}
              <div class="statline">range coverage {{ '%.0f' % c.coverage_pct }}% of global span</div>
              {% endif %}
              <div class="tags">
                <span class="tag">pair: {{ c.entry.pairing_signal }}</span>
                <span class="tag">aff: {{ c.entry.affinity_signal }}</span>
                <span class="print-tag {{ c.print_safety }}">{{ c.print_safety }}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="copyblock">
                <code>{{ c.entry.id }}</code>
                <button onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('  - id: {{ c.entry.id }}\n    status: approved')">copy approved</button>
              </div>
              {% if c.entry.notes %}<div class="notes"><strong>Notes.</strong> {{ c.entry.notes }}</div>{% endif %}
              {% if c.entry.reviewer_notes %}<div class="notes"><strong>Reviewer.</strong> {{ c.entry.reviewer_notes }}</div>{% endif %}
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

</div>
</body>
</html>
